{
  format: 1
  name: resource-digest-verified-at-load
  suite: scenario
  spec: ["#package-structure", "§4.1", "#history", "§19.5", "#annex-d", "§D.5"]
  note: '''
    Happy path for §4.1 $resources: descriptor with $path/$media/$sha256, entry
    bytes matching the declared digest. "Every declared digest is verified before
    activation" — here verification succeeds and the artifact activates. Uses the
    extension steps documented in NOTES.md.

    The model is incidental to the rule under test and carries a single OPTIONAL
    root member. §22.1 makes "field and shape types" hold in every committed
    state, and `none` is absence rather than a value (§5.5, A.1), so a
    NON-optional root member with no default and no `$seed`/`$bundle` value has no
    admissible genesis state (§5.1/§8.2): the load would then be refused for a
    reason that has nothing to do with `$resources`.
  '''
  tags: ["artifact"]

  package: {
    $liasse: 1
    $app: "t.invoice@1.0.0"
    $resources: {
      invoice_template: {
        $path: "resources/invoice.html"
        $media: "text/html"
        $sha256: "2163bddf11b2e116332448d10374d504f9508c148b72e5c9d970b88665330490"
      }
    }
    $model: {
      note: "text?"
    }
  }

  steps: [
    // sha256("<h1>Invoice</h1>") = 2163bddf...0490 — matches the declared digest
    { build_artifact: { as: "a1", files: { "resources/invoice.html": "<h1>Invoice</h1>" } } }
    { load_artifact: { from: "a1", expect: { outcome: ok } } }
  ]
}
